      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukiah%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Camas Land Company platted the town of Ukiah in August 1890.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukiah%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ukiah opened its first post office in September 1890 with Whiting serving as the first postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukiah%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Ukiah lies along Camas Creek, which flows west from the Blue Mountains and through the Umatilla National Forest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukiah%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Camas Creek, which runs through Ukiah, is a tributary of the North Fork John Day River.",
